diff --git a/docs/source/whats_new.rst b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
index 563f18f521..38f540af7f 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ Version 1.8.0 (2026-10-06)
 Enhancements
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
 - Add :class:`moabb.datasets.Wang2026Handwriting`, a Chinese handwriting-imagery dataset from Wang et al. (2026, Scientific Data, CC-BY 4.0; figshare, BIDS): 21 healthy adults in two handwriting-imagery tasks -- CCS-HI (five Chinese character strokes) and SV-HI (six Pinyin vowels) -- each recorded in two sessions, 40 trials of 4 s per class, 32-channel 10-10 EEG at 1 kHz. The two BIDS tasks share a session and carry no run entity, so the loader keys them by task; the release's ``trial_type`` labels are normalized to the class names and the two sessions with fewer valid trials (sub-06 ses-02 SV-HI, sub-13 ses-02 CCS-HI) are kept as released (:gh:`1244` by `LiQing`_).
-- Add standalone :class:`moabb.paradigms.CognitiveTask` for non-motor endogenous tasks (handwriting/stroke imagery, mental arithmetic, mental rotation, word generation, music imagery). It subclasses :class:`~moabb.paradigms.base.BaseParadigm` directly — not motor imagery — with MotorImagery-matching 8-32 Hz defaults, N-class event logic, and validity on both ``paradigm="cognitive"`` and the existing ``paradigm="imagery"`` tag (follows the Cued Cognitive Tasks branch of :gh:`1056`). :class:`moabb.datasets.Shin2017B` (mental arithmetic vs rest) and :class:`moabb.datasets.BNCI2024_001` (10-letter handwritten character task) flip to ``paradigm="cognitive"`` with a new ``summary_cognitive.csv`` table, updated docstrings/METADATA, and runtime/docs/test allowlists (neural-signature handler, bubble-plot colormap, metadata catalog checks).
+- Add standalone :class:`moabb.paradigms.CognitiveTask` for non-motor endogenous tasks (handwriting/stroke imagery, mental arithmetic, mental rotation, word generation, music imagery). It subclasses :class:`~moabb.paradigms.base.BaseParadigm` directly — not motor imagery — with MotorImagery-matching 8-32 Hz defaults, N-class event logic, and validity on both ``paradigm="cognitive"`` and the existing ``paradigm="imagery"`` tag (follows the Cued Cognitive Tasks branch of :gh:`1056`). :class:`moabb.datasets.Shin2017B` (mental arithmetic vs rest), :class:`moabb.datasets.BNCI2024_001` (10-letter handwritten character task) and :class:`moabb.datasets.Wang2026Handwriting` (Chinese stroke/vowel handwriting imagery) flip to ``paradigm="cognitive"`` with a new ``summary_cognitive.csv`` table, updated docstrings/METADATA, and runtime/docs/test allowlists (neural-signature handler, bubble-plot colormap, metadata catalog checks).
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.Dreyer2023` (and its ``A``/``B``/``C`` subclasses) now load their EEG from NEMAR's ``nm000250`` ``sourcedata/`` store when the download provider allows it, falling back to the OSF host exactly like other NEMAR-mirrored datasets; this stops MOABB's docs/example builds from failing on OSF's ``files.de-1.osf.io`` 429 rate limiting. ``get_subject_info()`` reads the demographic ``performance.csv`` from the store once it is published there, else falls back to OSF (:gh:`1237` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Add :class:`moabb.datasets.Yagan2023`, a P300 row-column speller dataset (Mendeley Data, CC-BY 4.0; 18 healthy subjects, 160-character copy-spelling in 10 blocks, 32-channel BrainVision EEG at 1 kHz, ~560k intensification events with an exact 2/13 target ratio per block). S14 target markers are stamped 2-3 ms after their flash in the released marker files, so each S1-S13 flash is relabelled ``Target``/``NonTarget`` by pairing it with any S14 within 10 ms (:gh:`1220` by `LiQing`_).
 - Document a download-free, paradigm-only metadata preflight using the existing ``MotorImagery.is_valid`` API, including explicit ``n_classes`` semantics and unknown evaluation compatibility; add a no-I/O regression test for the recipe (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
